\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Begone, unbelief; my Saviour is near,
\par And for my relief will surely appear:
\par By prayer let me wrestle, and He will perform;
\par With Christ in the vessel, I smile at the storm.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Though dark be my way, since He is my Guide,
\par 'Tis mine to obey, 'tis His to provide;
\par Though cisterns be broken and creatures all fail,
\par The word he hath spoken shall surely prevail.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. His love in time past forbids me to think
\par He'll leave me at last in trouble to sink;
\par While each Ebenezer I have in review
\par Confirms His good pleasure to help me quite through.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Why should I complain of want or distress,
\par Temptation or pain? He told me no less;
\par The heirs of salvation, I know from His word,
\par Through much tribulation must follow their  Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Since all that I meet shall work for my good,
\par The bitter is sweet, the medicine food;
\par Though painful at present, 'twill cease before long;
\par And then, O how pleasant the conqueror's song!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

